<title>SWITZERLAND: SNB leaves discount rate at one percent.</title>
<headline>SNB leaves discount rate at one percent.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Swiss National Bank (SNB) said it was leaving its discount rate at 1.00 percent after a regular weekly meeting of its three-member board.</p>
<p>&quot;No change,&quot; said an SNB spokesman in response to an enquiry.</p>
<p>The rate at current levels matches the historic low maintained from February 1978 to November 1979.</p>
<p>The rate was last changed when it was lowered from 1.50 percent on September 26.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial, +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
